<title>USA: Sinter buys Delco Remy's Powder Metal unit.</title>
<headline>Sinter buys Delco Remy's Powder Metal unit.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinter Metals Inc said it bought Delco Remy America Inc's Powder Metal Forge unit for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Powder Metal Forge makes forgings for high duty General Motors Corp parts, like connecting rods and transmission races, Sinter said.</p>
<p>Sinter acquired primarily Powder's manufacturing and related equipment, which it will move to a newly constructed site in Emporium, Pennsylvania, it said.</p>
<p>Under Sinter, Powder will continue to supply GM with parts, Sinter added.</p>
</text>
